1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:05,805
I keep my rank stitched on an old wool coat

2
00:00:06,807 --> 00:00:12,191
The thread is thin, but the colors never ran

3
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:19,719
We rode out to Warsong with a war cry in our throats

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:25,344
Now I'm an old man thinking back to when

5
00:00:26,466 --> 00:00:31,911
Those three a.m. queues and the dawn coming slow

6
00:00:33,994 --> 00:00:38,638
Every week another rung, one at a time

7
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:45,424
Calling out the flag runner, cheering every flag we stole

8
00:00:45,906 --> 00:00:51,891
Brothers on the bridge in Alterac, side by side

9
00:00:52,953 --> 00:00:58,277
Give me one more night of the long climb up

10
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:05,064
Fourteen ranks and we never got enough

11
00:01:06,366 --> 00:01:11,891
The spirit healer knew my face too well

12
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:18,598
I'd queue it all again, every fight where I fell

13
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:25,164
New standings posted every Tuesday dawn

14
00:01:26,066 --> 00:01:31,651
We'd check the ladder, grin, and queue back on

15
00:01:32,713 --> 00:01:38,477
Names on my friends list, gray a long, long while

16
00:01:39,319 --> 00:01:45,004
Got jobs and kids now, but one whisper'd make 'em smile

17
00:01:45,906 --> 00:01:51,350
Give me one more night of the long climb up

18
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:58,017
Fourteen ranks and we never got enough

19
00:01:59,339 --> 00:02:04,784
The spirit healer knew my face too well

20
00:02:05,005 --> 00:02:11,551
I'd queue it all again, every fight where I fell

21
00:02:12,232 --> 00:02:18,057
I don't miss the gear, I don't miss the gold

22
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:25,856
I miss the callouts and the jokes, and the lines we used to hold

23
00:02:25,906 --> 00:02:31,390
And I still stand beneath the colors that we bore

24
00:02:32,092 --> 00:02:38,077
If that horn blew tonight, I'd ride out once more

25
00:02:38,879 --> 00:02:44,383
Give me one more night of the long climb up

26
00:02:45,786 --> 00:02:51,070
One more week with my brothers would be enough

27
00:02:52,292 --> 00:02:57,797
The spirit healer knew my face too well

28
00:02:57,978 --> 00:03:04,523
I'd queue it all again, every fight where I fell

29
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:11,170
Every fight where I fell

30
00:03:12,412 --> 00:03:17,577
One more Tuesday, one more climb
